Tracked so this directory exists in every checkout BEFORE sbatch runs.

slurmstepd opens the batch --output/--error paths before it execs the job script, and SLURM does not
create their parent directories -- so the `mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR"` inside
sbatch_powered_closure_budget_probe.sh is far too late to help. Job 56355818 was submitted with the
sibling powered_closure/logs/ absent: it held a queue slot for hours and would have died at dispatch
with nothing written anywhere. Same trap, same fix, one directory over.

The probe's products deliberately live here rather than in powered_closure/ so that a diagnostic run
at a non-nominal training budget can never be mistaken for the gate's D2 evidence.
